strings.NOV_research_and_development_category_de:
The face of warfare has changed. Battles are no longer decided by massed infantry and thundering artillery, but by whoever can dominate the skies above contested ground. We have seen examples of this across the world, from South Africa to Indonesia to our own backyards.

If Russia is to become powerful again, she must not concede her own airspace to the enemy. The great powers of the world have spent years building their air forces, and our own armada pales in comparison in both size and sophistication. It is essential that we make up for lost time, and the best way to do that is by sponsoring any project that may help us achieve aerial supremacy.

The costs may be high, but they are nothing compared to what we will pay if we surrender the skies of the Motherland.

